# ZSpace T2: where U-Boot's persistent environment lives.
#
# U-Boot stores it as a file (`CONFIG_ENV_FAT_FILE="uboot.env"`) inside the FAT
# `boot` partition (`CONFIG_ENV_FAT_DEVICE_AND_PART=":3"` - partition 3 of the
# mmc device U-Boot booted from: mmc0/eMMC in the final layout, mmc1/SD on the
# card).  Userspace cannot address a file inside a FAT partition directly, and
# libubootenv cannot mount a partition, so t2-boot-commit.service mounts that
# partition at /run/t2-boot and the libubootenv tools read/write the file
# through this path (the path only exists while the unit has the mount up).
#
# CONFIG_ENV_SIZE is 0x1f000 (126976 bytes) in
# u-boot/configs/t2-rk3568_defconfig, and that is the size of the file itself
# (it includes the 4-byte CRC32 header).  U-Boot's `saveenv` and `fw_setenv`
# write exactly this blob, so both sides see the same `bootcount` /
# `upgrade_available` / `t2_fallback` values.
/run/t2-boot/uboot.env 0x0 0x1f000
